Library cards
=============


§ 1  Interpretation

In this document, unless the context otherwise requires:

1. Residence means one of in the city or outside the city.

2. Card means one of adult card, junior card, or no card.

3. Applicant consists of:
    - name — text
    - age — number
    - residence — Residence
    - has a guardian's consent — yes or no
    - number of overdue books — number


§ 2  Provisions

1. The applicant has overdue books if the applicant's number of overdue books is more than 0.

2. The applicant may get a library card if:
    (a) the applicant's residence is in the city;
    (b) any of the following:
        (i) the applicant's age is at least 16; or
        (ii) the applicant has a guardian's consent; and
    (c) it is not the case that the applicant has overdue books.

3. The card for the applicant is:
    | Condition                                                    | Result      |
    |--------------------------------------------------------------|-------------|
    | it is not the case that the applicant may get a library card | no card     |
    | otherwise, if the applicant's age is at least 16             | adult card  |
    | otherwise                                                    | junior card |


Coverage
left out: Ada
left out: Ben
